# Mintlify automatically ignores these files and directories:
# .git, .github, .claude, .agents, .idea, node_modules,
# README.md, LICENSE.md, CHANGELOG.md, CONTRIBUTING.md

# Draft content
drafts/
*.draft.mdx

# Internal engineering docs. These live under docs/ so they version with the
# code and stay reachable by the knowledge graph, but they are NOT part of the
# public docs site. Everything matched below must stay unpublished —
# architecture contracts, implementation plans, and QA maps are internal-only.
#
# Omission from docs.json navigation is NOT a publication boundary. A page left
# out of navigation is only hidden from the sidebar — it stays reachable by URL
# and can still be indexed. This file is the only thing that stops Mintlify from
# processing and serving a page.
#
# THE RULE: all new internal material goes under internal/. This list is frozen
# — scripts/ci/docs_publication_boundary.py (Code Style workflow) rejects any
# entry added to it. reborn/ is the one remaining legacy location: its path is
# load-bearing (architecture tests read contract files from it, and the
# reborn-e2e scope filters match it), so it moves into internal/ only when
# those consumers move with it. Entries may be removed as that happens, never
# added. The same check requires every .md/.mdx under docs/ to be in docs.json
# navigation, matched here, or carrying `hidden: true` frontmatter marking a
# deliberately unlisted public page.
internal/
reborn/